				\begin{document}$${{\rm{Cosine}}}\,{{\rm{similarity}}}(A,B)=\cos (\rho )=\frac{A\cdot B}{\parallel A\parallel \parallel B\parallel }.$$\end{document}Cosinesimilarity(A,B)=cos(ρ)=A⋅B∥A∥∥B∥.Furthermore, we define the coverage between A and B as:5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
