				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${{\rm{Coverage}}}(A,B)={\sum}_{i}{a}_{i}{{\mathbb{1}}}_{{b}_{i}\ \!\! > \!\! \ 0}$$\end{document}Coverage(A,B)=∑iai1bi>0To obtain the cosine similarity and coverage between MS/MS spectra, they need to be discretized along the m/z dimension. This is typically done by binning m/z values or by matching query and reference peaks and then assigning a dimension to each peak pair and each unmatched peak. The latter is specified in Equation (6), which defines the cosine similarity between the spectra SA and SB at a tolerance value t that determines whether two peaks match:6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
